{"step_index":1076,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T14:20:13Z","thinking":"**Inspecting Nginx Request Data**\n\nExamining the Nginx capture reveals a health check request. The request targets the health endpoint of the application. The host is `map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr`, and the `X-Forwarded-Port` is `9440`.\n\n\n**Identifying Duplicate Headers in Request**\n\nThe Nginx capture shows duplicate `Host`, `X-Forwarded-Proto`, and `X-Forwarded-Port` headers, which violates RFC 7230. Tomcat's strict adherence to this standard results in a `400 Bad Request` error when multiple `Host` headers are present. Examining the Nginx configuration reveals the cause: the `proxy_set_header` directives, combined with the default headers passed, are adding redundant headers to the proxied requests.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"/home/koby/.ansible/kssh th2-revproxyp-fe1 'curl -sS -i -k -H \\\"Host: foo\\\" -H \\\"Host: bar\\\" https://172.30.198.50:9443/centreon-map/api/latest/actuator/health'\"","Cwd":"\"/home/koby\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolAction":"\"Testing duplicate Host header against Tomcat\"","toolSummary":"\"Curl duplicate Host header to Tomcat\""}}]}
