{"step_index":1102,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T14:21:42Z","thinking":"**Identifying Split-Horizon Routing**\n\nThe external VIP address is unreachable from the current network, while the internal DMZ IP is reachable, suggesting a split-horizon DNS or routing configuration. External users access the service through a public VIP via the WAN, while internal users use a separate internal address. This setup is typical in many environments.\n\n\n**Analyzing Nginx Proxy Configuration**\n\nDuplicate `Host:` headers in the Nginx configuration are suspected of causing 400 Bad Request errors. Removing the `include` directive, or explicitly configuring headers, should eliminate the duplication.  These header conflicts often lead to unexpected behavior at the backend, which is causing these issues.\n\n\n**Examining Nginx Proxy Settings**\n\nThe configuration focuses on setting proxy headers like `X-Forwarded-For`, `X-Forwarded-Proto`, and `X-Forwarded-Host`, suggesting a reverse proxy setup. CORS (Cross-Origin Resource Sharing) headers are configured to allow requests from different origins, crucial for AJAX calls. The OPTIONS method handling, a preflight request, ensures proper CORS support.\n\n\n**Evaluating Nginx Header Inheritance**\n\nThe `add_header` directives within a `location` block do not inherit from the `server` block unless the `location` block *overrides* the `add_header`.  CORS headers defined within the `server` block will be inherited by the `location /` if it does not have its own `add_header` directives. For `OPTIONS` preflight requests within `location /`, custom CORS headers are needed.\n\n\n**Determining CORS Request Type**\n\nThe AJAX health check uses a `GET` request without custom headers, triggering a simple CORS request from the browser. The browser includes an `Origin` header with the request. The server accepts if the `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` matches or is `*`.\n\n**Evaluating Origin Header Handling**\n\nUsing `*` for `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` is valid when `withCredentials` is not set.  Using `$http_origin` or explicit origin checks is safer, especially for handling credentials.  If no `Origin` header exists, such as with `curl`, a map or `$http_origin` can provide flexibility.\n\n**Verifying Nginx Configuration Location**\n\n`map` directives cannot be placed within the `server` context.  They must reside within the `http` context or within a `server` block to function correctly, ensuring appropriate origin handling.\n\n\n**Confirming Public Health Check Access**\n\nThe health check endpoint is publicly accessible and does not use credentials based on JavaScript code and the endpoint response. Therefore, the current wildcard CORS configuration is validated.\n\n**Initiating Proxy Fix Validation**\n\nThe Nginx configuration file is being reviewed to test whether the duplicate `Host` header fix resolves the proxy issues. This aims to verify the direct impact of the header correction.\n\n\n**Identifying Header Duplication Issue**\n\nExamining the Nginx configuration, conflicting `Host` and `X-Forwarded-*` headers within the `location /` block are noted. Specifically, the included `proxy.conf` and explicitly defined headers are setting the same values. This likely causes issues with the backend. Removing this duplication can resolve any associated proxy errors.\n\n**Considering Configuration Consolidation**\n\nThe proposed fix aims to replace the included `proxy.conf` and duplicate header directives. The corrected configuration sets HTTP version and cache-bypassing correctly, in addition to the other header options. By consolidating these settings, the Nginx configuration should become cleaner. The new version will set proxy headers and ensure correct HTTP and websocket support with cache bypass logic.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"/home/koby/.ansible/kssh th2-revproxyp-fe1 \\\"echo '8&#JMl1Mwe0GyN' | sudo -S cp /etc/nginx/sites-available/03-map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf /etc/nginx/sites-available/03-map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf.bak.\\\\$(date +%F_%H%M%S)\\\"\"","Cwd":"\"/home/koby\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolAction":"\"Backing up Nginx vhost\"","toolSummary":"\"Backup 03-map config\""}}]}
