ows\\System32\\drivers\\etc\\hosts`)*\n+  Then reload Centreon Web and click **\"Test connection to server\"**.\n \n[diff_block_end]\n\nPlease note that the above snippet only shows the MODIFIED lines from the last change. It shows up to 3 lines of unchanged lines before and after the modified lines. The actual file contents may have many more lines not shown.","truncated_fields":["content"]}
{"step_index":1140,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T14:23:58Z","content":"The culprit has been captured, dissected, and eradicated.\n\nHere is the exact technical post-mortem and the fix deployed on **`th2-revproxyp-fe1`**.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Root Cause: The Duplicate `Host` Header Trap\n\nWhen testing through Nginx, Apache Tomcat was returning <span style=\"color:red;font-weight:bold;\">HTTP Status 400 – Bad Request</span>.\n\nBy sniffing the raw HTTP payload sent by Nginx to Tomcat, we uncovered duplicate headers:\n```http\nHost: map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr\nHost: map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr:9443\nX-Forwarded-Proto: http\nX-Forwarded-Proto: https\n```\n\n* **Why Nginx did this**: In Nginx, multiple `proxy_set_header` directives with the same key inside the same block **do not overwrite** each other — they are both injected. Including `nginxconfig.io/proxy.conf` while explicitly setting `proxy_set_header Host $http_host;` caused Nginx to inject **two distinct `Host:` lines**.\n* **Why Tomcat broke**: Tomcat complies strictly with **RFC 7230 / RFC 9112 Section 5.4**:\n  > *\"A server MUST respond with a 400 (Bad Request) status code to any request message that contains more than one Host header field.\"*\n\nDirect verification against Tomcat confirmed:\n* **Duplicate `Host` header** $\\rightarrow$ <span style=\"color:red;font-weight:bold;\">HTTP/1.1 400 Bad Request</span>\n* **Single clean `Host` header** $\\rightarrow$ <span style=\"color:green;font-weight:bold;\">HTTP/1.1 200 OK</span> (`{\"status\":\"UP\"}`)\n\n---\n\n### 2. The Remediation Applied on `th2-revproxyp-fe1`\n\nWe updated [`/etc/nginx/sites-available/03-map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf`](file:///etc/nginx/sites-available/03-map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf):\n\n1. **Eliminated Duplicate Headers**: Removed the generic include and declared a clean, single-pass proxy header block:\n   ```nginx\n   proxy_http_version         1.1;\n   proxy_cache_bypass         $http_upgrade;\n   proxy_set_header Upgrade   $http_upgrade;\n   proxy_set_header Connection $connection_upgrade;\n\n   proxy_set_header Host              $http_host;\n   pro\n<truncated 885 bytes>\nPTIONS') {\n       add_header 'Access-Control-Allow-Origin' '*' always;\n       add_header 'Access-Control-Allow-Methods' 'GET, POST, OPTIONS, PUT, DELETE' always;\n       add_header 'Access-Control-Allow-Headers' 'DNT,User-Agent,X-Requested-With,If-Modified-Since,Cache-Control,Content-Type,Range,Authorization' always;\n       add_header 'Access-Control-Max-Age' 1728000;\n       add_header 'Content-Type' 